---
code: lint-no-lintable-files
when-fires: dorc lint was given nothing lintable. cli/main.rs lint_command. No params.
why: 27R section 8b: zero files is OPERATIONAL, never clean - a vacuous pass is the CI failure mode the exit trichotomy exists to prevent.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- lint-no-lintable-files && mise run loom:promote -- lint-no-lintable-files`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all lint-no-lintable-files` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=webhost.sh
error[lint-no-lintable-files]: Dorc was given no files to lint; an empty lint
counts as a failure, not a clean pass.
